.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt LOG 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm log
.Nd show, stream and configure the system log
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm show
.Op Fl -last Ar time | Fl -start Ar date
.Op Fl -end Ar date
.Op Fl -info
.Op Fl -debug
.Op Fl -predicate Ar predicate
.Op Fl -style Ar style
.Nm
.Cm stream
.Op Fl -level Ar default | info | debug
.Op Fl -predicate Ar predicate
.Op Fl -style Ar style
.Op Fl -timeout Ar seconds
.Nm
.Cm config
.Fl -subsystem Ar name
.Fl -mode Ar level:default | level:info | level:debug
.Nm
.Cm config
.Fl -subsystem Ar name
.Fl -reset
.Nm
.Cm config
.Fl -status
.Nm
.Cm erase
.Fl -all
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads the messages that programs send with
.Xr os_log 3 ,
as
.Nm logd
keeps them.
Default, error and fault messages are kept on disk, in
.Pa /var/db/diagnostics ;
info messages are kept in memory, and debug messages only for subsystems
whose level is debug.
Users other than root see only their own processes' messages.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm show
Prints the kept messages, oldest first.
.Fl -last
takes a time such as 30s, 5m, 2h or 1d;
.Fl -start
and
.Fl -end
take a local date, as
.Dq 2026-11-03 23:40:01 .
Info messages are shown with
.Fl -info ,
info and debug with
.Fl -debug .
.It Cm stream
Prints messages as they arrive, until interrupted or for
.Fl -timeout
seconds.
.It Cm config
Sets a subsystem's level (root only): which of the info and debug
messages it keeps.
.Fl -reset
gives it the system's level again (info);
.Fl -status
lists the subsystems with a level of their own.
.It Cm erase
Removes every kept message (root only).
.El
.Pp
A
.Ar predicate
is an
.Vt NSPredicate
over
.Va process ,
.Va processIdentifier ,
.Va userIdentifier ,
.Va subsystem ,
.Va category ,
.Va messageType
(default, info, debug, error or fault),
.Va eventMessage ,
.Va threadIdentifier ,
.Va activityIdentifier
and
.Va timestamp ,
for example
.Dq subsystem == \e"org.example\e" AND messageType == error .
A
.Ar style
is default, compact, syslog or json.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/db/diagnostics" -compact
.It Pa /var/db/diagnostics
the messages kept on disk
.It Pa /var/db/logd/levels
the subsystems' levels
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr os_log 3 ,
.Xr syslog 1
